":"application","question":"For $A(x,y)=(x,0)$ on $\\mathbb{R}^2$, what is the range?","options":["The $x$-axis $\\{(x,0)\\colon x\\in\\mathbb{R}\\}$.","The $y$-axis $\\{(0,y)\\colon y\\in\\mathbb{R}\\}$.","Only $\\{(1,0)\\}$.","All of $\\mathbb{R}^2$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"607549ed1b608ac13eedbd9c","time_limit":25},{"id":"la_hq_b3_range_of_a_linear_map_007","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What is the range of the zero map $Z\\colon V\\to W$?","options":["$\\{0\\}$.","The empty set.","The whole domain $V$.","The whole codomain $W$ always."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"465de84f2030af3fffa1f1b0","time_limit":20},{"id":"la_hq_b3_range_of_a_linear_map_008","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"For $A(t)=(t,2t)$ from $\\mathbb{R}$ to $\\mathbb{R}^2$, which vector lies in the range?","options":["$(2,1)$","$(0,1)$","$(3,5)$","$(3,6)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b245ba106c4b6eb0af3bfa6c","time_limit":20},{"id":"la_hq_b3_range_of_a_linear_map_014","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"For $A\\colon\\mathbb{R}^2\\to\\mathbb{R}$ given by $A(x,y)=x-y$, what is the range?","options":["$\\mathbb{R}$","$\\{(t,t)\\colon t\\in\\mathbb{R}\\}$","$\\mathbb{R}^2$","$\\{0\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9db607665b55b33cdf876027","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_hq_b3_range_of_a_linear_map_015","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"For $A(x,y,z)=(x,y)$ from $\\mathbb{R}^3$ to $\\mathbb{R}^2$, is $A$ surjective?","options":["Yes, every $(a,b)\\in\\mathbb{R}^2$ is reached by $(a,b,0)$.","No, because $z$ is discarded.","No, because the domain has more coordinates.","Yes, but only the zero vector is reached."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4b14e17882565c2b135473c3","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_hq_b3_range_of_a_linear_map_017","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Can the range equal the codomain even when the kernel is not $\\{0\\}$?","options":["No, an onto linear map must also be injective","Yes, for maps onto a codomain of smaller dimension","Yes, but only when the domain and codomain are equal","Yes, but only if the codomain is larger than the domain"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ec341fdd06922cc7d2bfc44e","time_limit":40},{"id":"la_hq_b3_range_of_a_linear_map_018","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why is saying “$w\\in\\operatorname{range}A$” an existence statement?","options":["It means $w$ is a scalar.","It means every $v\\in V$ satisfies $Av=w$.","It means there exists some $v\\in V$ with $Av=w$.","It means $w$ lies in the kernel."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ac0482cc55327bc0fed57872","time_limit":40},{"id":"la_hq_b3_range_of_a_linear_map_020_curated20261027_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"For $\\boldsymbol{A}=\\begin{pmatrix}1&2\\\\0&0\\end{pmatrix}$, what is the range of $\\boldsymbol{x}\\mapsto\\boldsymbol{A}\\boldsymbol{x}$ on $\\mathbb{R}^2$?","options":["$\\operatorname{span}((1,0))$","$\\operatorname{span}((1,2))$","$\\mathbb{R}^2$","$\\operatorname{span}((2,-1))$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d09599780ebf9eb9a4e0a464","time_limit":30}]}}